[00:00.00] 作词 : John Newton
[00:01.00] 作曲 : John Newton
[00:03.53]
[00:03.68]Amazing grace, how sweet the sound
[00:16.90]That saved a wretch like me
[00:30.64]I once was lost but now I'm found
[00:47.00]Was blind, but now, I see
[00:59.60]
[01:01.30]T'was grace that taught my heart to fear
[01:13.82]And grace, my fears relieved
[01:27.01]How precious did that grace appear
[01:42.39]The hour I first believed
[01:59.72]
[02:23.28]Through many dangers, toils and snares
[02:33.67]We have already come
[02:43.67]T'was grace that brought us safe thus far
[02:53.79]And grace will lead us home
[03:03.56]
[03:04.25]When we've been there ten thousand years
[03:14.55]Bright shining as the sun
[03:24.98]We‘ve no less days to sing God's praise
[03:40.87]Than when we first begun
[03:52.46]
[04:13.76]I once was lost but now I'm found
[04:26.65]Was blind, but now, I see
